    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d709">

                <pb facs="0861" n="737" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg737"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.71637/8: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Cable</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-09-30T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 30,
                                1921—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>162. For General Crowder:</p>
                <p>Department’s No. 161, September 30, 2 p.m., and letter September 21.<anchor
                        n="58" xml:id="d709-f1"/></p>
                <p>Postmaster General informs Department that indebtedness of Cuban Government to
                    Post Office Department on account of postal money orders is now approximately
                    $500,000. Postmaster General states that it is extremely embarrassing for the
                    postal money order system of the United States to finance that of Cuba in a sum
                    aggregating half a million dollars; that the money order fund is greatly
                    embarrassed by the non-payment of this amount rightfully due under the terms of
                    the Convention.</p>
                <p>In view of the above, and of the positive statement of President Zayas to
                        you<anchor n="59" xml:id="d709-f2"/> that the amount due would be paid in
                    fifteen days from August 25th, the Department desires that in case the loan of
                    $5,000,000 is negotiated in accordance with the Department’s telegram of
                    September 30, 2 p.m., and in case the amount due is not sooner paid, it be
                    specifically provided in the loan contract that this sum be paid out of the
                    proceeds of the loan.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
